  "description": "You can buy an identically\nequipped Fuji in either of two frame materials, steel (Finest) or aluminum\n(Finest-AL). A Finest-AL isn't made from just any aluminum, it's custom\nbutted and tapered 7005 alloy. Good stuff.\n\nThe Finest-AL's frame is lighter and higher-tech than the Finest's. It\nis newly \"re-tuned\" to increase its ride compliance, to eliminate\nany hint of aluminum's hard ride. Gone. No hard ride from the bike's aero-shaped\nCro-Moly fork, either. The Shimano Sora parts and CRP bar and stem are\nknown for dependability and lightness. The brake/shift levers on the handlebars\nare ready for the addition of a Shimano Flight Deck computer, a font of\nuseful information.\n\nHow do you choose between a Finest and a Finest-AL? If you're planning\nto install a luggage rack or to take trips with saddlebags, I'd buy the\nsteel Finest. It's easier to mount those things on the Finest's frame.\n\nIf you're doing your club's weekend rides, and those rides are faster\nthan you'd really like, I'd buy a Finest-AL. The aluminum bike will feel\nfaster, more like a racing bike. Maybe you'll feel faster too, more like\na bike racer.",
